prompt.on_input:
{{ background_context }}
<session_input hook="{{ input.hook }}" time="{{ input.time }}">
{% for item in input.items %}
{% if item.is_todo_update %}
{{ item | render_format: "event.xml" }}
The task you are working on was updated (the reason and the whole new task are above). Compare it with what you have done: adjust the next steps, undo or redo what no longer fits, stop tasks you no longer need with `cancel_task`, and report against the new acceptance criteria.
{% endif %}
{% if item.is_task_result %}
{{ item | render_format: "event.xml" }}
This is the end of task {{ item.source.id }}: the complete result, as its call would have returned it. Use it; do not run the command again.
{% endif %}
{% if item.is_tick %}
<tick timer="{{ item.source.id }}">{{ item.summary }}</tick>
Your work is still running. Go on with something that does not depend on it, or reply with one or two sentences on where things stand (that closes this Turn); `cancel_task` stops a task you no longer need.
{% endif %}
{% if item.is_nudge %}
<runner_notice>{{ item.summary }}</runner_notice>
{% endif %}
{% if item.is_other_event %}
{{ item | render_format: "event.xml" }}
{% endif %}
{% if item.is_child_end %}
{{ item | render_format: "event.xml" }}
{% endif %}
{% if item.is_child_needs_input %}
{{ item | render_format: "event.xml" }}
{% endif %}
{% if item.is_msg %}
{{ item | render_format: "message.xml" }}
{% endif %}
{% endfor %}
When every task you started has ended and the results are verified, finish with `report` (is_end: true).
</session_input>

